# [fork change] Line endings.
#
# The `shared-*.timelog` fixtures are pinned by SHA-256 -- in the desktop
# suite (ganttproject-tester/.../TimeJournalTest.kt) and, identically, in
# the Android one (android/gantt-core/.../TimeJournalTest.kt). The digests
# are the whole mechanism that keeps the two implementations of the hour
# journal from drifting apart, so the bytes on disk have to be the bytes in
# the object store on every platform.
#
# Without this line a clone made with Git's Windows default
# (core.autocrlf=true) gets CRLF in the working tree and six checks in
# TimeJournalTest turn red on code that is perfectly correct.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto`. That would not fix this at all --
# it marks the fixtures as text, which is exactly what invites the
# conversion -- and it would renormalise six unrelated files that are
# committed with CRLF today (the two gradlew.bat launchers,
# ganttproject.bat, ganttproject.nsi.tpl and two bundled LICENSE texts).
*.timelog -text
